## API reference

### Dialog

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `default_open:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Open on connect. |
| `modal:` | `Boolean` | `true` | Trap focus and make the page inert (`show()` instead of `showModal()` when false). |
| `dismissible:` | `Boolean` | `true` | Close on a click outside the card. |

Events: `ui--dialog:open-change` with `{ open }`; dispatch `ui--dialog:open` / `ui--dialog:close` to drive it.

### DialogContent

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `close_button:` | `Boolean` | `true` | The × in the corner. |
| `close_label:` | `String` | "Close" | Its accessible name (translated). |
| `backdrop:` | `Boolean` | `true` | The dimmed, blurred layer behind. |
| `frame:` | `Boolean` | `true` | A frosted frame around the card (needs the backdrop). |

`class:` styles the card - `sm:w-100`, `sm:w-200`, a fixed `h-*`. `DialogHeader`, `DialogTitle` (`<h2>`),
`DialogDescription` (`<p>`), `DialogBody` and `DialogFooter` lay it out; `DialogTrigger` and `DialogClose` take a
block with an argument to put their attributes on your own Button.

## Accessibility

- The card is a `role="dialog"` labelled by the title and described by the description; focus is trapped and
  returns to the trigger.
- Escape closes the frontmost dialog; the enter / exit transitions honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
